  <GeneDef ParentName="DZ_CentaurBody_DireBase">
    <defName>DZ_CentaurBody_Direhorse</defName>
    <label>direhorse body</label>
    <description>Carriers of this gene have the four-legged lower body of a direhorse in place of regular human legs. The shaggy coat pattern varies from carrier to carrier, and the heavy frame makes them larger and sturdier than a baseliner.

Produces 30 direhorse wool every 25 days, modified by body size.</description>
    <iconPath>BSCE/Icons/Direhorse</iconPath>
    <displayOrderInCategory>800</displayOrderInCategory>
    <geneClass>BigAndSmall.ProductionGene</geneClass>
    <modExtensions>
      <li Class="BigAndSmall.ProductionGeneSettings">
        <product>MA_DirehorseWool</product>
        <frequencyInDays>25</frequencyInDays>
        <baseAmount>30</baseAmount>
        <progressName>Growing direhorse wool</progressName>
        <saveKey>DZ_DirehorseWoolProduction</saveKey>
      </li>
    </modExtensions>
    <statFactors>
      <SM_BodySizeMultiplier>1.4</SM_BodySizeMultiplier>
      <ConstructionSpeed>1.05</ConstructionSpeed>
    </statFactors>
  </GeneDef>

  <GeneDef ParentName="DZ_CentaurBody_DireBase">
    <defName>DZ_CentaurBody_Wooly</defName>
    <label>wooly direhorse body</label>
    <description>Carriers of this gene have the four-legged lower body of a wooly direhorse in place of regular human legs. Bred for the cold, this lineage grows far larger and heavier than other centaurs.

Produces 30 direhorse wool every 20 days, modified by body size.</description>
    <iconPath>BSCE/Icons/Direhorse_White</iconPath>
    <displayOrderInCategory>801</displayOrderInCategory>
    <geneClass>BigAndSmall.ProductionGene</geneClass>
    <modExtensions>
      <li Class="BigAndSmall.ProductionGeneSettings">
        <product>MA_DirehorseWool</product>
        <frequencyInDays>20</frequencyInDays>
        <baseAmount>30</baseAmount>
        <progressName>Growing direhorse wool</progressName>
        <saveKey>DZ_WoolyWoolProduction</saveKey>
      </li>
    </modExtensions>
    <statFactors>
      <SM_BodySizeMultiplier>1.70</SM_BodySizeMultiplier>
      <ConstructionSpeed>1.10</ConstructionSpeed>
    </statFactors>
  </GeneDef>

</Defs>
